tmka:GT-0081 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual says use is relevant to a number of questions and lists them. Something that feeds into an answer rather than being the answer is a relevant_factor."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "relevant_factor" ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Use plays a different role under each provision it touches. If the taxonomy is meant to type a concept by its role, this concept may need several typings."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0081" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> .

tmka:GT-0082 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 7(3) makes authorised use count as the owner's use, so it feeds the questions use feeds — capability to distinguish, prior use, ownership — rather than answering one of its own."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "relevant_factor" ;
    tmk:confidence 6.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether control is itself a test that should be a separate concept."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0082" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> .

tmka:GT-0083 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 8(1) defines the authorised user as a person — the one who uses the mark under the owner's control. The concept record already separates the person from the use, and it is the person this record types."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "process_role" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'authorised user' the party and 'authorised use' the fact should both be concepts. If they should, typing only the party leaves the more examinable half of the pair unheld by anything."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0083" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s8> .

tmka:GT-0084 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 6 defines the registered owner as the person in whose name the mark is registered. A party, identified by an entry rather than constituted by one."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "process_role" ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether registered owner and applicant are one party at two stages or two concepts. Part 19B treats the registration as personal property held by that person, and a role typing carries none of that."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0084" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/registered-owner> .

