tmka:GT-0112 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "A treaty, administered by WIPO's International Bureau. Not a rule the Act makes: Australian practice gives effect to it. Keeping that visible is CLAUDE.md rule 5 applied one level up — the Manual is practice and not law, and the Protocol is neither Australian law nor Australian practice."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "external_instrument" ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether a two-member group is worth having at all, and if it is, whether the Nice Classification belongs in it beside a treaty. Those are the only two members and they are not obviously the same kind of thing."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0112" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> .

tmka:GT-0113 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Australian half of a Madrid registration — examined much as a domestic application is, which is why Parts 26 to 31 keep referring to it. A thing the process operates on."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "This is the record in the 53 most likely to be in the wrong group. If IRDA belongs with the Madrid Protocol, external_instrument holds three and the boundary between a scheme and the things it produces needs stating explicitly."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0113" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> .

tmka:GT-0114 tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Madrid equivalent of a registered trade mark, and citable against a domestic application under section 44. A thing."@en-AU ;
    tmk:conceptGroup "subject_matter" ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The same boundary as GT-0113. Holding this concept apart from 'registered trade mark' is what lets a citation search reach both, so a merge would cost more than the tidiness gains."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GT-0114" ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> .

