tmkc:GC-0059 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual sets out a two-part process — ordinary signification, then the likelihood that other traders would legitimately wish to use the mark — and sorts every mark examined into one of three categories on the answer."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "inherent adaptation"@en-AU,
        "inherent capacity to distinguish"@en-AU,
        "inherently adapted to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "inherent adaptation to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the question and its two-part method in terms. The concept is separate from capability because the Act treats inherent adaptation as one input to capability and use as the other, and the three-category sort in Part 22.3 only makes sense against inherent adaptation alone."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'inherent capacity to distinguish' really is a synonym. The Manual uses 'capacity' and 'adaptation' in adjacent sentences and an expert may hold them apart."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0059" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)(a)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(4)(a)> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo tmkc:GC-0006 ;
    tmk:notLabel "acquired distinctiveness"@en-AU,
        "capable of distinguishing"@en-AU,
        "evidence of use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/3%231~1> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0059 .

tmkc:GC-0081 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual calls use a concept fundamental to trade mark law and lists the questions it bears on: capability to distinguish, honest concurrent or prior use, ownership. Section 6 says its meaning is 'affected by' subsections 7(1), (2) and (3) — which is not the same as being defined by them."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "trade mark use"@en-AU,
        "use"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "use of a trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the concept's place in the scheme and the Act tells us where its meaning is affected. Held as one concept with the specialised uses — authorised, prior, honest concurrent — as separate records beside it, because each answers a different question under a different provision."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'use in the course of trade' should be the preferred label. Section 17 makes the course of trade part of what a trade mark is, and the bare word 'use' may be too wide for a vocabulary that also holds authorised use and prior use."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0081" ;
    tmk:isDefinedIn <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s17>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s7> ;
    tmk:notLabel "authorised use"@en-AU,
        "evidence of use"@en-AU,
        "honest concurrent use"@en-AU,
        "prior use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/use-of-a-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19A/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0081 .

tmkc:GC-0084 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProcessRole ;
    rdfs:comment "Defined by the Register: the person in whose name the mark is registered. That is narrower than ownership at common law, and the Manual's Part 19B treats the registration as personal property held by that person."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "owner of the trade mark"@en-AU,
        "registered proprietor"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined by the Act in terms; the Manual supplies the property characterisation the definition sits inside."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'owner of the trade mark' is safe as an alt_label. The Act uses that phrase in section 8 for a mark that need not be registered, so the alt_label may be too wide."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0084" ;
    tmk:isDefinedIn <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/registered-owner> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s21(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/registered-owner> ;
    tmk:notLabel "applicant"@en-AU,
        "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "predecessor in title"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/registered-owner>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part19B/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0084 .

tmkc:GC-0085 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Load-bearing in two places at once: section 41(5) makes a predecessor's use count as the applicant's for distinctiveness, and section 44(4) does the same for prior use. The section 6 definition itself is a stub that continues into a list."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "predecessor in title"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Act states the consequence in terms in section 41(5); the section 6 definition is a stub whose text does not carry the substance, so the evidence is drawn from the operative provision instead."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the concept should carry the section 6 list as narrower concepts. The stub continues into subparagraphs this record does not reach."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0085" ;
    tmk:isDefinedIn <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/predecessor-in-title> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(5)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(4)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/predecessor-in-title> ;
    tmk:notLabel "assignment"@en-AU,
        "authorised user"@en-AU,
        "registered owner"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0085 .

tmkc:GC-0091 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:RelevantFactor ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 41(3)(b) makes use 'before the filing date' the thing that can rescue a mark with no inherent adaptation, so the filing date is not merely administrative."@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "filing date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The section 6 definition is a stub continuing into a list, so the evidence is drawn from section 41(3)(b), where the date does operative work."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part10/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be a Part 10 or Part 11 passage that states how a filing date is set."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0091" ;
    tmk:isDefinedIn <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/filing-date> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s6/filing-date> ;
    tmk:notLabel "date of registration"@en-AU,
        "priority date"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0091 .

tmkc:GC-0102 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "A formal objection by a third party. The Manual notes that any person may oppose but that the opponent is generally somebody affected — which is a practice observation rather than a standing requirement, and the record keeps it in notes for that reason."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "opposition proceedings"@en-AU,
        "opposition to registration"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms at the head of the Manual's Part on the subject."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'any person may oppose' should be in the record rather than the notes. It is a statement about standing and belongs in a relationship record if anywhere."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0102" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s52>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.2> ;
    tmk:mustOccurWithin <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r5.13> ;
    tmk:notLabel "hearing"@en-AU,
        "rectification"@en-AU,
        "removal for non-use"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part46/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0102 .

tmkc:GC-0105 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "A court remedy, not a Registrar's one: the amendment or cancellation results from an order of a prescribed court. That is what separates it from every other correction mechanism in the Act."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "rectification"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "rectification of the Register"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Defined in terms, with the court requirement in the same two sentences."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part42/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Nothing specific."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0105" ;
    tmk:isPerformedBy tmkc:GC-0115 ;
