    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part33/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0108 .

tmkc:GC-0113 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "The Australian half of a Madrid registration. It is examined much as a domestic application is, which is why the Manual's Parts 26 to 31 keep referring to it, and it becomes a protected international trade mark rather than a registered trade mark."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "IRDA"@en-AU,
        "international registration designating Australia (IRDA)"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "international registration designating Australia"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_inferred" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Regulations define the term by pointing at another regulation whose text this record does not quote, so the basis is inferred rather than explicit. It is held because 86 Manual passages use the abbreviation and the vocabulary could not read them."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 6e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The evidence. This record's statutory citation is a pointer, not a definition, and the definition it points at should replace it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0113" ;
    tmk:isDefinedIn <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/international-registration-designating-australia> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/irda> ;
    tmk:notLabel "international registration"@en-AU,
        "protected international trade mark"@en-AU,
        "trade mark application"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/irda> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0113 .

tmkc:GC-0120 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:LegalTest ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's third category and the hardest to overcome: only use before the filing date sufficient to make the mark in fact distinguish will do it. The Manual's list of examples — pictorial representations, geographical names, laudatory words — is the practical content of the category."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "not to any extent inherently adapted to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "no inherent adaptation to distinguish"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states the category and exemplifies it in one sentence. Held for the same reason as the first category."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/6%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The missing middle category — limited inherent adaptation but not prima facie capable, the Manual's Part 22.5. This pass holds the outer two and not the middle, which is an omission rather than a judgement."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0120" ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)(a)> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41(3)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "inherent adaptation to distinguish"@en-AU,
        "prima facie capable of distinguishing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part22/6%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0120 .

tmkc:GC-0121 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:ExternalInstrument,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The largest Part of the Manual by chunk count — 743 of 2,460 — and the one most easily confused with the similarity question. Part 26 says in terms that classification does not determine similarity."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "classes"@en-AU,
        "classification"@en-AU,
        "the Nice Classification"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "classification of goods and services"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Held mainly to carry the near-miss: a third of the Manual is classification and the single most valuable thing the vocabulary can say about it is that it does not answer the section 44 question."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part14/1%231~1> ;
