tmkc:GC-0114 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:SubjectMatter ;
    rdfs:comment "The Madrid equivalent of a registered trade mark, and section 44's note 4 makes it citable against a domestic application. Holding it apart from 'registered trade mark' is what lets a citation search reach both."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "protected international trade mark designating Australia"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "protected international trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 44's note names the term and states its effect on examination, which is the operative fact. The Regulations' own definition is a pointer, as with IRDA."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 7e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part60/1/1/1> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "The definition source is a Part 60 passage about the Protocol generally rather than about protection specifically."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0114" ;
    tmk:hasStatutoryBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s111> ;
    tmk:isDefinedIn <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s189A/protected-international-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2/protected-international-trade-mark>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/protected-international-trade-mark> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r17A.2>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r2.1/protected-international-trade-mark> ;
    tmk:notLabel "IRDA"@en-AU,
        "international registration"@en-AU,
        "registered trade mark"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0114 .

tmkc:GC-0092 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "Section 31 gives examination two subjects and only two: whether the application was made in accordance with the Act, and whether there are grounds for rejecting it. Section 33 then makes acceptance the default unless the Registrar is satisfied of one of those."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "examine and report"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "examination"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "Section 31 states the duty and its two subjects in one sentence. Held because the whole corpus is an examination manual and the vocabulary had no word for the activity it describes."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8.5e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether the definition source should be a Part 5 or Part 6 passage about the examination process rather than Part 20.5 on grounds."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0092" ;
    tmk:hasStatutoryBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s174> ;
    tmk:isPerformedBy tmkc:GC-0044,
        tmkc:GC-0115,
        tmkc:GC-0116 ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s31>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s42(b)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "expedited examination"@en-AU,
        "hearing"@en-AU,
        "opposition"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s31> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0092 .

tmkc:GC-0096 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:LegalConcept,
        tmk:ProceduralStep ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual's own gloss is the useful part: the acceptance period is 'set in abeyance'. That distinguishes it from an extension of time, which lengthens a period rather than suspending it."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "defer acceptance"@en-AU,
        "deferment"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "deferment of acceptance"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual defines it in terms and contrasts it implicitly with the ordinary acceptance period."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/1%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether abeyance and extension really are different in effect, or only in procedure. The record asserts the first on the strength of one word."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0096" ;
    tmk:hasStatutoryBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s37(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.13(4)> ;
    tmk:isPerformedBy tmkc:GC-0115,
        tmkc:GC-0116 ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s36>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s37(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.12> ;
    tmk:mustOccurWithin <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.14(3)(e)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "acceptance"@en-AU,
        "extension of time"@en-AU,
        "lapsing"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part17/1%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0096 .

tmkc:GC-0053 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:GroundOfRefusal,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual treats the grounds as a closed set fixed by the Act and Regulations. Whether a formality failure under paragraph 33(1)(a) is a 'ground for rejection' in the same sense as sections 39-44 is a real question the passage leaves open."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "ground of rejection"@en-AU,
        "grounds for rejecting"@en-AU,
        "grounds for rejection"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "ground for rejection"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states in terms that the Act and Regulations contain all the grounds, and section 33(3) makes the Registrar's satisfaction that a ground exists the trigger for rejection. The concept is therefore the corpus's own, not a label imposed on it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether a failure of the formality requirements under paragraph 33(1)(a) belongs inside this concept or beside it. The Manual's Part 10 treats formalities separately and section 33 lists them separately, which argues for beside."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0053" ;
    tmk:hasStatutoryBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s41>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s43>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(1)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.15>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMR1995/r4.15A> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33(1)(b)> ;
    tmk:notLabel "ground for revocation"@en-AU,
        "ground of opposition"@en-AU,
        "objection"@en-AU ;
    tmk:origin "authored" ;
    tmk:reviewStatus "unreviewed" ;
    tmk:sourcePassage <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s33>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part20/5%231> ;
    tmk:typedBy tmka:GT-0053 .

tmkc:GC-0068 a skos:Concept,
        tmk:Exception,
        tmk:LegalConcept ;
    rdfs:comment "The Manual grounds this in the commercial realities that make acceptance proper notwithstanding a real risk of deception or confusion. It is the most open-textured of the three ways round section 44."@en-AU ;
    skos:altLabel "other circumstances making it proper to accept"@en-AU ;
    skos:inScheme tmkc:scheme-s43 ;
    skos:prefLabel "other circumstances"@en-AU ;
    tmk:authoredBy "claude-opus-5" ;
    tmk:authoredDate "2026-09-09"^^xsd:date ;
    tmk:authoringBasis "corpus_explicit" ;
    tmk:authoringReasoning "The Manual states what the paragraph turns on in one sentence. Held separately from honest concurrent use because paragraph 44(3)(b) is an alternative to 44(3)(a), not a gloss on it."@en-AU ;
    tmk:confidence 8e-01 ;
    tmk:definitionSource <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMM/Part28/4%231> ;
    tmk:expertShouldCheck "Whether 'notwithstanding a real risk of deception or confusion' should appear in the concept at all. It is the Manual's gloss on Bali No. 2 rather than the statutory test, and it is doing a lot of work in this record."@en-AU ;
    tmk:goldRecord "GC-0068" ;
    tmk:hasStatutoryBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177(2)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s177(2)(b)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(3)>,
        <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(4)> ;
    tmk:legislativeBasis <https://data.ipaustralia.gov.au/tmk/ref/TMA1995/s44(3)(b)> ;
    tmk:mayGiveRiseTo tmkc:GC-0006 ;
    tmk:notLabel "conditions and limitations"@en-AU,
        "honest concurrent use"@en-AU,
        "prior use"@en-AU ;
